{"id":"chatcmpl-a7012a56c39d2871","object":"chat.completion","created":1791523761,"model":"gemma-4-31b-it-qat-w4a16-ct","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"The AI agent is investigating a bug in `src/requests/utils.py` where the `super_len` function returns the character count for strings instead of the byte count, leading to incorrect `Content-Length` headers for non-ASCII characters.\n\n**Key Progress:**\n*   **Reproduction:** The agent initially encountered a false positive because their reproduction script was using the installed `requests` library instead of the local source code. After correcting the script to use `/workspace/src`, the agent successfully reproduced the issue (e.g., a string containing \"🚀\" resulted in a `Content-Length` of `1` instead of `4`).\n*   **Root Cause Identification:** The agent confirmed that `super_len` relies on `len(o)`, which in Python returns the number of characters for string objects.\n*   **Proposed Solution:** The agent intends to modify `super_len` to encode strings to UTF-8 before calculating their length, aligning with the encoding used elsewhere in the library (e.g., in `_encode_params`).\n\n**Unresolved Tasks:**\n*   **Impact Analysis:** The agent is currently using `grep` to find all occurrences of `super_len` to ensure that changing its behavior for strings will not introduce regressions in other parts of the application.\n*   **Implementation:** Once the impact is verified, the agent will implement the fix in `src/requests/utils.py`.","refusal":null,"annotations":null,"audio":null,"function_call":null,"tool_calls":[],"reasoning":"*   The AI agent is continuing the investigation into the `super_len` function in `src/requests/utils.py`.\n    *   The goal is to ensure `Content-Length` correctly reflects the number of bytes for strings, not the number of characters.\n    *   Previous confusion: A reproduction script initially seemed to pass (returned 4), but the agent discovered it was importing the *installed* `requests` library instead of the *local* version in `/workspace/src`.\n    *   Once the reproduction script was corrected to use the local source code, it failed as expected (returned 1 for \"🚀\"), confirming the bug.\n    *   The agent has identified that `super_len` uses `len(o)`, which for strings returns the character count.\n    *   The agent proposes updating `super_len` to encode strings to UTF-8 before calculating the length, noting that other parts of the codebase (like `_encode_params`) use UTF-8.\n    *   The agent is now planning to check other usages of `super_len` using `grep` to ensure that encoding strings to UTF-8 in `super_len` won't cause regressions.\n\n    *   Summary of conversation.\n    *   Focus on key information and decisions.\n    *   Unresolved questions/tasks.\n    *   Concise and captures the essence."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop","stop_reason":106,"token_ids":[100,45518,107,236829,139,818,12498,8726,563,15374,506,10622,1131,506,2165,12666,236779,3469,236929,1292,528,2165,2857,236786,48921,236786,13364,236761,2551,21233,107,140,236829,139,818,5671,563,531,5330,2165,4795,236772,8615,236929,15195,22136,506,1548,529,17234,573,16587,236764,711,506,1548,529,7579,236761,107,140,236829,139,40488,19381,236787,562,32029,8948,14877,10012,531,1786,568,204138,236743,236812,779,840,506,8726,11788,625,691,68112,506,808,63007,236829,2165,48921,236929,9427,5205,529,506,808,6047,236829,3567,528,86072,44484,236786,2857,21233,107,140,236829,139,14946,506,32029,8948,691,32107,531,1161,506,2263,3738,3393,236764,625,8428,618,4275,568,204138,236743,236770,573,623,242015,3959,49378,506,13582,236761,107,140,236829,139,818,8726,815,8385,600,2165,12666,236779,3469,236929,6178,2165,3469,236769,236748,188733,837,573,16587,7623,506,2872,1527,236761,107,140,236829,139,818,8726,46515,31652,2165,12666,236779,3469,236929,531,41193,16587,531,92916,236772,236828,1680,31236,506,3861,236764,28830,600,1032,4688,529,506,219734,568,5282,2165,23